From 546549b40457c94cf0cfa6ff21408e69e609a7f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phase14 audit <audit@local>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 11:41:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 17/20] feat(authorship): bylines credit functions, not named
 individuals
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Owner decision 2026-09-02 ("待决策项以 rfidak.com 的口径为准", D-06). rfidak.com
— the RFID brand of the same legal entity — names no individuals: articles
carry an editorial-team byline and the company is described by function
(international sales, RF / production engineering, quality control).
proudtek.com follows the same model because the four named authors could
not be evidenced (Phase 4 T9 / K-14).
- src/content/authors: peter-zhang, nancy-wu, mia-li and sam-yao retired;
  editorial-board -> 'Proud Tek Editorial Team', proudtek-engineering ->
  'Proud Tek RF / Production Engineering'; records carry type: Organization
- editorial-authority-ld.ts: Article.author / reviewedBy emit Organization
  nodes (description = role, parentOrganization = the site Organization)
  for function records; Person only for a record with a verifiable profile
- article-author-map.ts emptied (every snapshot article falls back to the
  editorial team); registry/schema/type updated accordingly
- about/leadership-banner.svg: founder node replaced by the legal entity and
  its functions
The editorial JSON slugs, EXPERT_AUTHORS and llms.txt attribution follow in
the next commits.
